IMPORT prelude

-- Methodist Episcopal Location Board Ordinance 1908 (Singapore) -- who the Corporation "The Secretary of the Trustees of the Methodist
-- Church in Singapore" is (s 2(1)) and how a successor becomes "duly qualified" (s 4), what the Ordinance empowers it to do (s 2(2), (3)),
-- how its deeds are validly sealed and signed (s 3), which land it took over from whom and subject to what (s 5 and the Schedule), and
-- whose rights the Ordinance leaves alone (s 6).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MELBO1908.txt. The deposit says the edition
-- "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021 and comes into operation on 31 December 2021". The amendment
-- annotations in the body are "[15/1954]" under s 2(1), "[15/1954; S(NS) 177/59]" under s 4(1) and "[7/97]" under s 6. The Ordinance
-- is dated 31 July 1908.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0238 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- The Ordinance is six sections and a Schedule, so the whole of it is in scope. For a person outside the Church it matters in two
-- places: dealing with the Corporation over land (buying, leasing, lending: ss 2(3), 3, 4) and title to the 25 parcels listed in the
-- Schedule (s 5, s 6).
--
-- NOT ENCODED: s 1 (short title); the preamble (recitals, not enactment); the content of s 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property
-- Act 1886, to which s 3(1) refers (whether a power of attorney has been "deposited" under it is taken as a stated fact); the land
-- descriptions, boundaries and areas in the Schedule's first column, other than which item lies where; the names in the third column
-- (whether a person is "specified in the third column" is a stated fact); the Corporation's internal governance and the trust for the
-- Malaysia Mission, about which the Ordinance says nothing beyond s 5(2).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Methodist Episcopal Location Board Ordinance 1908 -- the Corporation`

§§ `2(1) and 4 -- who is the Corporation, and when a successor is duly qualified`

-- s 2(1): "The said William Thomas Cherry and his successors for the time being in the office of Secretary of the said Board of
-- Building and Location duly qualified as hereinafter provided shall be a body corporate, hereinafter called the Corporation", with
-- perpetual succession under the name "The Secretary of the Trustees of the Methodist Church in Singapore" and a corporate seal.
-- s 4(1): "No successor of the said William Thomas Cherry in the office of Secretary of the Trustees of the Methodist Church in
-- Singapore shall be deemed to be duly qualified as aforesaid unless and until he has caused an extract from the minutes of the
-- Trustees of the Methodist Church in Singapore appointing him such Secretary, certified as correct by the Chairman of the Board, to be
-- filed in the office of the Minister, and unless and until a notification of such filing has appeared in the Gazette."
-- s 4(2): "Such notification shall be sufficient evidence of the appointment, and that the person named therein is duly qualified as by
-- this Ordinance is required."
--
-- Four things, all needed: appointment by the Trustees' minutes, the Chairman's certificate on the extract, filing with the Minister,
-- and the Gazette notification of the filing. Until all four, an appointed Secretary is not part of the Corporation. s 2(1) still speaks
-- of the Secretary of "the said Board of Building and Location", while s 4 speaks of the Secretary of the Trustees; the encoding follows
-- s 4 for the appointment (the office the 1954 amendment gave the Corporation's name). "The Board" whose Chairman certifies is not
-- identified in the text; it is read as the Trustees (an inference).
DECLARE Successor HAS
    `is appointed Secretary by the minutes of the Trustees` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the extract is certified correct by the Chairman` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the extract is filed in the office of the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the filing is notified in the Gazette` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the successor` IS A Successor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is duly qualified` IF
        `the successor`'s `is appointed Secretary by the minutes of the Trustees`
    AND `the successor`'s `the extract is certified correct by the Chairman`
    AND `the successor`'s `the extract is filed in the office of the Minister`
    AND `the successor`'s `the filing is notified in the Gazette`

-- s 4(2) makes the notification itself "sufficient evidence" of appointment and qualification: the encoding asks only whether it has
-- appeared. "Sufficient", not "conclusive": contrary proof is not modelled.
GIVEN `the successor` IS A Successor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Gazette notification is sufficient evidence of qualification` IF
    `the successor`'s `the filing is notified in the Gazette`

§§ `2(2) and 2(3) -- what the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to do`

-- s 2(2): "The said seal may from time to time be broken, changed, altered and made anew as to the Corporation seems fit."
-- s 2(3): "The Corporation may acquire, purchase, take, hold and enjoy movable and immovable property of every description, and may
-- sell, convey, assign, surrender and yield up, mortgage, demise, re-assign, transfer or otherwise dispose of any movable and immovable
-- property vested in the Corporation upon such terms as to the Corporation seem fit."
--
-- The powers of disposal reach only property "vested in the Corporation". The Ordinance contains no clause letting the Corporation sue
-- or be sued; whether the general law of corporations supplies that capacity is outside the text and not encoded.
DECLARE Power IS ONE OF
    `use and change its corporate seal`
    `acquire or purchase property`
    `hold and enjoy property`
    `sell or convey property`
    `mortgage property`
    `demise property`
    `transfer or otherwise dispose of property`
    `sue or be sued`

GIVEN `the power` IS A Power, `the property is vested in the Corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance empowers the Corporation to` IF
    CONSIDER `the power`
    WHEN `use and change its corporate seal` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `acquire or purchase property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `hold and enjoy property` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `sell or convey property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `mortgage property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `demise property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    WHEN `transfer or otherwise dispose of property` THEN `the property is vested in the Corporation`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `3 -- sealing and signing the Corporation's instruments`

-- s 3(1): "All deeds, documents and other instruments requiring the seal of the Corporation shall be sealed with the seal of the
-- Corporation in the presence of the said William Thomas Cherry or his attorney, duly authorised by a power of attorney deposited under
-- section 48 of the Conveyancing and Law of Property Act 1886, or in the presence of his successor for the time being in the office of
-- Secretary of the Trustees of the Methodist Church in Singapore or his attorney duly authorised as aforesaid, and shall also be signed
-- by the said William Thomas Cherry or his attorney or his said successor or his said attorney."
-- s 3(2): "Such signing shall be and be taken as sufficient evidence of the due sealing of such deeds, documents and other instruments."
--
-- Three things: the seal, affixed in the presence of the Secretary or a deposited attorney, and signed by the Secretary or such an
-- attorney (witness and signer need not be the same person on the words). s 3(1) names the successor "for the time being in the office";
-- unlike s 2(1) it does not say "duly qualified". On the words, a Secretary appointed by the Trustees but not yet gazetted under s 4
-- may witness and sign; that literal reading is encoded and flagged in NOTES.md.
DECLARE Officer IS ONE OF
    `the Secretary for the time being, duly qualified`
    `the Secretary for the time being, appointed but not yet gazetted`
    `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney`
    `an attorney whose power of attorney is not deposited`
    `a Trustee who is not the Secretary`
    `nobody`

DECLARE Instrument HAS
    `is sealed with the Corporation seal` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sealed in the presence of` IS AN Officer
    `signed by` IS AN Officer

GIVEN `the officer` IS AN Officer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is the Secretary or a deposited attorney` IF
    CONSIDER `the officer`
    WHEN `the Secretary for the time being, duly qualified` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Secretary for the time being, appointed but not yet gazetted` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an attorney under a deposited power of attorney` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is executed as section 3 requires` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Secretary or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `sealed in the presence of`)
    AND `is the Secretary or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

-- s 3(2): the signing is evidence of "the due sealing". Read as requiring that the instrument bears the seal and is signed by a person
-- s 3(1) allows to sign; who witnessed the sealing does not enter.
GIVEN `the instrument` IS AN Instrument
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the signature is sufficient evidence of due sealing` IF
        `the instrument`'s `is sealed with the Corporation seal`
    AND `is the Secretary or a deposited attorney` (`the instrument`'s `signed by`)

§§ `5 and the Schedule -- the land vested in the Corporation`

-- s 5(1): the persons "or their executors or administrators" and the Financial Board "mentioned in the third column of the Schedule, in
-- whom are vested the respective estates and interests mentioned in the second column of the Schedule in the lands ... specified in the
-- first column of the Schedule are hereby divested of such estates and interests."
-- s 5(2): "Such estates and interests and all other estates and interests of such persons and body in the said lands ... are hereby
-- vested in the Corporation as sole trustee for the Malaysia Mission of the Methodist Episcopal Church subject to the mortgages
-- mentioned in the second column of the Schedule, but with full powers as such trustee to deal with the said property as provided in
-- section 2."
--
-- Only Schedule land, and only the interests of the third-column holders (or their executors or administrators). s 5(2) takes "all
-- other estates and interests" of those holders in that land, not only the one in the second column.
DECLARE Holding HAS
    `the land is listed in the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder is specified in the third column for it` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the holder is executor or administrator of such a person` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the holding` IS A Holding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 5 vests it in the Corporation` IF
        `the holding`'s `the land is listed in the Schedule`
    AND (    `the holding`'s `the holder is specified in the third column for it`
         OR  `the holding`'s `the holder is executor or administrator of such a person`)

-- The Schedule has 25 items under three headings: "LAND IN SINGAPORE" (items 1-16), "LAND IN PENANG" (items 17-21) and "LAND IN
-- PROVINCE WELLESLEY" (items 22-25).
DECLARE Place IS ONE OF
    `Singapore`
    `Penang`
    `Province Wellesley`
    `not a Schedule item`

GIVEN `the item` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A Place
DECIDE `the Schedule item lies in` IS
    IF `the item` < 1 OR `the item` > 25 THEN `not a Schedule item`
    ELSE IF `the item` <= 16 THEN `Singapore`
         ELSE IF `the item` <= 21 THEN `Penang`
              ELSE `Province Wellesley`

-- The second column names two mortgages: items 2 and 3 are subject to "a mortgage dated 12 June 1907" (registered in Volume CCLXXIX,
-- No. 180), and items 17, 18 and 19 to "a mortgage dated 17 May 1907" (registered in Volume CCXLVI, No. 14). s 5(2) vests the land
-- "subject to the mortgages". No other item mentions a mortgage.
GIVEN `the item` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Corporation takes the item subject to a Schedule mortgage` IF
        `the item` EQUALS 2 OR `the item` EQUALS 3
    OR  `the item` EQUALS 17 OR `the item` EQUALS 18 OR `the item` EQUALS 19

-- Leaseholds in the second column, by start year and term: item 1 sub-items (ii)-(iv) "999 years from 18 August 1885" (item 1(i) is
-- fee simple); item 2 "99 years from 31 January 1859"; item 5 "999 years from 17 March 1828"; item 8 "99 years from 1 September 1840";
-- item 10 "999 years from 7 August 1832"; item 11 "999 years from 15 August 1894". The year in which the term ends is start year plus
-- term; 0 means the item is not leasehold. The arithmetic is the encoder's, not the text's.
GIVEN `the item` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the Schedule lease ends in year` IS
    IF `the item` EQUALS 1 THEN 1885 + 999
    ELSE IF `the item` EQUALS 2 THEN 1859 + 99
         ELSE IF `the item` EQUALS 5 THEN 1828 + 999
              ELSE IF `the item` EQUALS 8 THEN 1840 + 99
                   ELSE IF `the item` EQUALS 10 THEN 1832 + 999
                        ELSE IF `the item` EQUALS 11 THEN 1894 + 999
                             ELSE 0

§§ `6 -- whose rights are saved`

-- s 6: "Nothing in this Ordinance shall affect the rights of the Government or of any bodies politic or corporate, or of other person or
-- persons than are specified in the third column of the Schedule."
--
-- Only those specified in the third column can be affected. The executors and administrators whom s 5(1) divests are not "specified in
-- the third column"; read literally, s 6 saves their rights. The encoding follows each section's words and leaves the tension visible
-- (see NOTES.md). Mortgagees are not in the third column, so their rights are saved, which agrees with "subject to the mortgages" in s 5(2).
GIVEN `is specified in the third column of the Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Ordinance may affect their rights` IF
    `is specified in the third column of the Schedule`
